#
# Counter-example for math:DiagonalDegenerateFiltrationConstraint (issue #1527): a
# math:MultiparameterFiltration whose stage carries a math:multiIndex whose two
# components — at DISTINCT positions 0 and 1 — share the SAME math:componentValue node,
# a diagonal (t, t) index that is functionally dependent and genuinely one-parametric
# despite the 2-tuple. The cross-node equality constraint (two components at distinct
# indices carrying the same math:componentValue) fires — shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent
# (math:DiagonalDegenerateFiltration).
# ISOLATION: the filtration IS complete for its frame (math:filtrationIndexPoset and a
# math:hasFiltrationStage present), so math:IncompleteMultiparameterFiltration stays silent;
# a math:multiIndex IS present, so math:CollapsedMultiparameterFiltration cannot fire; the
# shared value math:RationalValue is well-formed (numerator and denominator present). So
# EXACTLY ONE finding.
# Back-reference: math:DiagonalDegenerateFiltration (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecMultiparameterDiagonal).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:diagonal a math:MultiparameterFiltration ;
    math:filtrationIndexPoset ex:grid ;          # completes the frame
    math:hasFiltrationStage ex:stage .           # completes the frame

ex:grid a math:MathematicalObject .

ex:stage a math:FiltrationStage ; math:multiIndex ex:index .

# Both coordinates, at indices 0 and 1, point at the SAME value node ex:tCoord — the
# functionally dependent diagonal (t, t).
ex:index a math:Vector ; math:hasComponent ex:coord0 , ex:coord1 .
ex:coord0 a math:VectorComponent ; math:atIndex 0 ; math:componentValue ex:tCoord .
ex:coord1 a math:VectorComponent ; math:atIndex 1 ; math:componentValue ex:tCoord .

ex:tCoord a math:RationalValue ; math:numerator 4 ; math:denominator 1 ; math:isExact true .
